  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Blue Mountain — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Blue Mountain.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Blue Mountain.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Blue Mountain"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Blue Mountain" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #000b1d   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #e5ecf3   crema     — primary text (16.54:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #00b5b5   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #000b1d   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #052544   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #e5ecf3   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #e5ecf3   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #f86572   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #001228   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #00b5b5   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #001228   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #f86572   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #60a563   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #ef912d   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #49accf   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #b181e5   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #00b5b5   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #c3cfdc   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #8797a9   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #f55e6c   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #6dba70   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #ebaa1f   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #49c1ea   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #bd87f6   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #00caca   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #00b5b5;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #e5ecf3   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
